---
import DockerTable from "./fragments/DockerTable.astro";
import CloudflareIngress from "./fragments/CloudflareIngress.astro";
import PocketBaseList from "./fragments/PocketBaseList.astro";
import DnsInstrument from "./fragments/DnsInstrument.astro";
import { host } from "../content/homelab";
---

<section class="section homelab" aria-labelledby="homelab-title">
  <div class="frame homelab__frame">
    <div class="homelab__head">
      <h2 id="homelab-title" data-reveal>It runs on a laptop.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="homelab__text">
      <p>
        An old laptop that stopped being fast enough for anything else, with
        Ubuntu Server on it. Everything runs in Docker, and everything was put
        back automatically the last time the power went out.
      </p>
      <p class="homelab__fact">{host.uptimeDays} days since the last reboot.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="homelab__panel">
      <DockerTable />
    </div>

    <div class="homelab__text">
      <p>
        Nothing is port-forwarded. Every service is published through a
        Cloudflare Tunnel, so the only thing the router exposes is nothing at
        all, and the certificates renew themselves.
      </p>
      <p class="homelab__fact">Zero ports open on the router.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="homelab__panel">
      <CloudflareIngress />
    </div>

    <div class="homelab__text">
      <p>
        One PocketBase instance holds the data behind everything I build: job
        applications, training sessions, video pipeline runs. Six collections,
        one backup path, no spreadsheet anywhere.
      </p>
      <p class="homelab__fact num">5 108 records, backed up nightly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="homelab__panel">
      <PocketBaseList />
    </div>

    <div class="homelab__text">
      <p>
        And the part that is actually about support: DNS. Most of what a helpdesk
        does all day is a DNS question wearing a costume. Type a hostname and see
        what my Pi-hole does with it.
      </p>
      <p class="homelab__fact">13 regex rules across three blocklists.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="homelab__panel homelab__panel--instrument">
      <DnsInstrument />
    </div>

    <p class="homelab__note">
      {host.os}. Every number on this page was read off the machine, not
      estimated.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
